{"name":"Ageing Barrel","hex":"#6a5b4e","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ageing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of age"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth, UK, Australia, New Zealand, and South Africa standard spelling of aging."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ageing"},{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"},{"title":"Ageing","blocks":[{"text":"Ageing is the process of becoming older. The term refers mainly to humans, many other animals, and fungi; whereas for example, bacteria, perennial plants and some simple animals are potentially biologically immortal. In a broader sense, ageing can refer to single cells within an organism which have ceased dividing, or to the population of a species."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ageing","wikidata":"Q332154"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/500px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/500px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional oak barrels made by Chilean cooperage Tonelería Nacional","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg/500px-Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg/1280px-Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg/500px-Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mackmyra barrels at Häckeberga Castle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Castle_Rock_Brewery_-_Nottingham_-_England_-_2004-11-04.jpg/500px-Castle_Rock_Brewery_-_Nottingham_-_England_-_2004-11-04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi